═╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═══╪═
 catch dangerous migrations
 before they reach production

  migrail reads your migrations the way the database runs them. It reports
  statements that lock tables, rewrite them or break code that's still running,
  and shows how to fix each one.

  [1mUsage[m
    migrail <command> [flags]

  [1mCommands[m
    [1mcheck       [mCheck SQL migrations for locks, rewrites and breaking changes
    [1mexplain     [mExplain what a rule detects and how to fix it
    [1mrules       [mList every rule with its severity and category
    [1mschema      [mPrint the JSON schema for .migrail.yaml
    [1mversion     [mPrint the migrail version and build details

  [1mFlags[m
        [1m--ascii[m           use ASCII symbols instead of Unicode
        [1m--color string[m    use color: auto, always or never (default "auto")
        [1m--no-hyperlinks[m   don't print clickable file links
        [1m--theme string[m    color theme: auto, dark, light or mono
                          (default "auto")

  Run migrail <command> --help for details on a command.
